// Title: Ruby Inline Command Execution
// Sigma ID: 20a5ffa1-3848-4584-b6f8-c7c7fd9f69c8
// Status: test | Level: medium
// Author: Nasreddine Bencherchali (Nextron Systems)
// Date: 2023-01-02 | Modified: -
// ATT&CK: execution, T1059
// Description: Detects execution of ruby using the "-e" flag. This is could be used as a way to launch a
//   reverse shell or execute live ruby code.
// False positives:
//   - Unknown
// References:
//   - https://pentestmonkey.net/cheat-sheet/shells/reverse-shell-cheat-sheet
//   - https://www.revshells.com/
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/05d1031f537e830b76da53bae2400c5814c89165/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_ruby_inline_command_execution.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, microsoft_xdr schema)

DeviceProcessEvents
| where (FolderPath endswith "\\ruby.exe" or ProcessVersionInfoOriginalFileName =~ "ruby.exe") and ProcessCommandLine contains " -e"
